<title>JAPAN: NEC to invest extra $285 mln in PB-NEC.</title>
<headline>NEC to invest extra $285 mln in PB-NEC.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>NEC Corp said on Monday that it would invest an additional $285 million in Packard Bell NEC (PB-NEC) to help the U.S. firm strengthen its business in office-use personal computers.  </p>
<p>The payment would be made on Monday and take NEC's total investment in the U.S. firm to $1.04 billion, including asset transfers worth $300 million, he said.</p>
<p>NEC's stake in PB-NEC would rise to 51.9 percent from 43.94 percent, although the shares to be acquired on Monday were stocks without voting rights, so its stake with voting rights would remain at 19.84 percent, the spokesman said.</p>
</text>
